  "purpose": "The fixed set of accepted changes that #125's three counts are computed over. Enumerated and pinned so the counts re-run to the same numbers rather than being recomputed against whatever the default branches hold later.",
  "enumeration": {
    "method": "Per frame: walk the default branch newest-first in the stated unit, keep a change only if it adds at least one line matching source_glob, stop at limit. Added lines are git numstat additions, which is the same quantity gate/changeset.py attributes as added_lines.",
    "limits": {
      "AdarGit008/mcgyvr": 100,
      "pallets/click": 30,
      "immerjs/immer": 30
    },
    "window": "mcgyvr is enumerated over its complete history (29 first-parent merges, 20 of which add source). click and immer were enumerated inside a depth-120 shallow clone taken at the pinned commit, so their frames are the most recent qualifying commits within that window and NOT a sample of the whole history. immer yields 27 rather than 30 because the window ran out, not because a filter rejected three.",
    "excluded": "Merge commits in the external frames (their changes are attributed to the commits they merge). Deletions and binary changes, which carry no added lines by construction. Test and documentation additions, which are not the rung's territory."
  },
